<article class="env-exercise" id="02DW">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02DW">Exercise <span data-tag="02DW">111.23.1</span>.</a> Suppose that $A$ is a ring and $M$ is an $A$-module. Let $f_ i$, $i \in I$ be a collection of elements of $A$ such that </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A) = \bigcup D(f_ i).  \]
</div>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
Show that if $M_{f_ i}$ is a finite $A_{f_ i}$-module, then $M$ is a finite $A$-module. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Show that if $M_{f_ i}$ is a flat $A_{f_ i}$-module, then $M$ is a flat $A$-module. (This is kind of silly if you think about it right.) 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>